msgid ""
"Combat experience has led to you being able to block multiple attacks at a time.\n"
"\n"
"+1 block attempt."
msgstr ""
"戦闘訓練を重ね、一度に複数の攻撃をブロックできるようになりました。\n"
"\n"
"回避発動+1"

msgid ""
"Combat is much easier if you can fight just one monster at a time.  You can sometimes "
"kite singled-out zombies, drawing them to a place of your choosing.  Use doorways as a "
"choke point or stand behind a window and strike as the zombies slowly climb through.  "
"Be wary - in numbers, they will push through anyway.  Never be afraid to just run if "
"you can outpace your enemies.  Irregular terrain, like forests, may help you lose "
"monsters."
msgstr ""
"常に1対1で敵と戦うよう心掛ければ、戦闘はずっと楽になります。ゾンビを孤立させて釣り出し"
"ましょう。戸口でモンスターを詰まらせ、窓枠を乗り越えようと苦労しているゾンビを反対側か"
"ら攻撃しましょう。ゾンビはどんな場所も無理やり通ろうとするため、油断は禁物です。敵より"
"素早く動けるなら、恐れずに逃げましょう。森林などの不規則な地形は敵を撒くのに便利です。"

msgid ""
"Combat skills in the Melee and Ranged categories are quite specialized, focused on "
"specific damage types and firearm flavors.  The Crafting and Interaction categories "
"are more general, each covering a potentially wide range of techniques and abilities."
msgstr ""
"戦闘スキルは「近接戦闘」と「遠距離戦闘」に分類され、それぞれが特定の攻撃方法や銃器の種"
"類に割り当てられた、かなり専門的な技能です。一方で、「アイテム製作」と「動作」に分類さ"
"れるスキルはより一般的なものであり、それぞれ幅広い技術や能力に割り当てられています。"

msgid "Combat took place in close quarters, focusing on melee skills…"
msgstr ""
"スカベンジャー部隊は閉所での接近戦を余儀なくされました。近接戦闘スキルが試されます..."

msgid "Combination Strike"
msgstr "連携撃"

msgid "Come Fly the Treacherous Skies"
msgid_plural "copies of Come Fly the Treacherous Skies"
msgstr[0] "本(一般/裏切りの空を舞え)"

msgid ""
"Come a little closer, I don't want to make too much noise.  You smell much nicer than "
"what I'm used to.  Someone in trouble banged on the door that night, she said she was "
"desperate, she had a baby, her home had burned down and her drugs were gone and there "
"were monsters in the streets.  We figured she was on drugs, but we couldn't turn them "
"away so we gave them food and let them stay in the barn."
msgstr ""
"もう少し近くへ来てくれ。あまり大声を出したくない。大丈夫、普段嗅いでる悪臭よりずっとマ"
"シだ。その日の夜にうちのドアを叩く奴がいた。その女は死に物狂いだった。妊娠してて、家が"
"全焼して、薬も切れて、通りには怪物がいるなんて言い出すんだ。ヤク中かと思ったが追い返す"
"こともできなかったから、食べ物を与えて、納屋に泊めてやった。"

msgid "Come back later when you have the money, then we'll talk."
msgstr "金が用意出来たらまた来い。話はそれからだ。"

msgid ""
"Come back when you get a chance Marshal.  We really need get in touch with rest of the "
"region."
msgstr "気が変わったらまた来てくれ、執行官。他の生存者との連絡手段は必要になる。"

msgid "Come back when you get a chance, we could use a few good men."
msgstr "また顔を出してほしい、君のような人間がいると非常に助かる。"

msgid "Come back when you get a chance, we really need to start reclaiming the region."
msgstr "気が変わったらまた来てくれ。ここの環境を改善していかないと。"

msgid "Come back when you get a chance."
msgstr "気が変わったら、また来てくれ。"

msgid "Come back when you get a chance.  We need skilled survivors."
msgstr "機会があればまた来てくれ。技術を持った生存者は常に必要だ。"

msgid "Come on <name_g>, you're better than this."
msgstr "うわぁ、<name_g>、マトモな人だと思っていたのに。"

msgid "Come on man, I just need a smoke."
msgstr "なあちょっと、タバコが欲しいんだ。"

msgid "Come on!  What're we doing here?!"
msgstr "おいおい！こんなところで何をするんだ！？"

msgid "Come on, Dave.  We're friends.  I won't use this against you or anything."
msgstr "頼むよ、デイブ。友達だろう。他人に話したりはしない。"

msgid "Come on, best push on."
msgstr "さあ、話の後は活動の時間だ。"

msgid "Come on, don't leave me hanging."
msgstr "おいおい、ちゃんと話してくれよ。"

msgid "Come on, talk to me!"
msgstr "こっちに来て、話し合おう！"

msgid "Come on, we're friends."
msgstr "いいじゃないか、友達だろう。"

msgid "Come on, you love hearing yourself talk."
msgstr "頼むよ、喋るのが好きなんだろ。"

msgid "Come on.  We got stuff to do."
msgstr "そろそろ切り上げよう。やることがある。"

msgid "Come with me, if you want to live."
msgstr "生き延びたいなら、私と一緒に来るんだ。"

msgid ""
"Come with me.  Maybe you're not the greatest adventurer, but it's better than living "
"here."
msgstr ""
"私と一緒に行こう。あなたは最高の冒険者ではないかもしれないけど、ここに住み続けるよりは"
"マシだ。"

msgid "Come with me.  We can help each other out."
msgstr "一緒に来てくれ。互いに助け合おう。"

msgid "Comfortable"
msgstr "快適"

msgid "Comfortably Fluid"
msgstr "肉体の流動性"

msgid ""
"Coming from a word meaning \"broken corn kernels\" in the language of the "
"Narragansett, it is a popular dish during hard times and Thanksgiving in New England.  "
"Incorporating maize and beans (or a similar legume), it is cheap and made from common "
"ingredients."
msgstr ""
"「割れたトウモロコシ粒」を意味するナラガンセット族の言葉に由来する、困窮しているときや"
"感謝祭の宴でよく食べられるニューイングランドの料理です。トウモロコシと豆(またはそれに類"
"するマメ科植物)が入っており、特別な材料も要らず安く作れます。"

msgid "Coming through!"
msgstr "通らせて！"

msgid "Coming to Terms with America: Essays on Jewish History, Religion, and Culture"
msgid_plural ""
"copies of Coming to Terms with America: Essays on Jewish History, Religion, and Culture"
msgstr[0] "本(一般/アメリカとの和解:ユダヤの歴史、宗教、文化エッセイ)"

msgid "Commence irradiation sequence"
msgstr "照射シーケンス開始"

msgid "Commercial"
msgstr "商業施設"

msgid ""
"Commercial fertilizer tends to be made from ammonium nitrate, which is also usable as "
"an explosive.  Try looking for some around the abandoned farms."
msgstr ""
"大抵の化学肥料の原料は硝酸アンモニウムだ。この物質は火薬にも転用できる。放棄された農場"
"を探してみてはどうだろう。"

msgid "Common Cold"
msgstr "風邪"

msgid "Common Cold Antibodies"
msgstr "風邪抗体"

msgid "Common cold antibodies in your bloodstream prevent you from catching common cold."
msgstr "血中に風邪の抗体ができており、風邪への感染を防ぎます。"

msgid ""
"Common in nature as an insect venom, this substance has a number of industrial uses "
"such as preservation and manufacturing."
msgstr ""
"自然界では昆虫毒として一般的なこの物質は、防腐処理や製造業など、様々な産業用途をもって"
"います。"

msgid "Common manure, could probably be used to make some great fertilizer."
msgstr "一般的な動物の糞尿です。効果の高い化学肥料の材料になりそうです。"

msgid "Common roe from an unknown fish."
msgstr "何らかの魚が産み落とした一般的な魚卵です。"

msgid ""
"Commonly known as pinkeye, this minor infection can be treated with antihistamines.  "
"If it's bacterial, antibiotics may help, but you can't tell without a lab analysis."
msgstr ""
"一般的に感染性結膜炎と知られるこの軽い感染症は、抗ヒスタミン薬で治療できます。 細菌性で"
"あれば抗生物質が効くかもしれませんが、検査をしなければ分かりません。"

msgid ""
"Commonly seen tucked away in the holsters of police officers, certain military "
"professionals, and civilian shooters, this is a larger, older, service-oriented "
"version of the popular Glock 19.  Similarly firing the 9x19mm cartridge and using "
"higher capacity magazines, it performs largely the same, but due to the longer "
"magazine well, it can't fit magazines shorter than the standard 17-round ones."
msgstr ""
"警察官、または一部の軍人や一般人のホルスターに収まっている姿をよく見かける、人気の高い"
"グロック19より大きく古めかしい軍用拳銃です。グロック19と同様に9x19mm弾を発射し、より大"
"容量の弾倉を使った場合も性能はほぼ互角ですが、弾倉挿入部が長いため、標準の17発弾倉より"
"短い弾倉は装填できません。"

msgid ""
"Commonly used by hunters, this single-edged sheath knife is designed for cutting and "
"skinning game rather than combat."
msgstr ""
"主に狩人が用いる片刃の鞘付きナイフです。戦闘用というよりも、獲物の解体や皮を剥ぐ用途で"
"設計されています。"

msgid ""
"Commonly used in electronics prototyping, this solderless breadboard is a small brick "
"of plastic filled with hundreds of holes connected by internal electrical busses.  "
"With a few components and scraps of wire, you could quickly build a circuit on this, "
"if you know what you're doing."
msgstr ""
"電子機器の試作によく使われる、いわゆる「はんだ付け不要ブレッドボード」です。プラスチッ"
"ク製の小さな板に数百個の穴が開いており、内部がバスで繋がっています。いくつかの部品とワ"
"イヤーの切れ端、そして知識があれば、すぐに回路を作ることができます。"

msgid "Communed with the trees"
msgstr "木々と交信した"

msgid "Comoros flag"
msgid_plural "Comoros flags"
msgstr[0] "国旗(ｺﾓﾛ)"

msgid ""
"Compact, svelte, and lightweight, this Leen bolt-action rifle packs the same features "
"of larger sporting weapons into a backpack-sized package.  Possessing an adjustable "
"buttstock, a detachable magazine-based system, and a quick-swap barrel that can be "
"exchanged to accommodate the firing of .223 Remington or 7.62x39mm Soviet ammunition, "
"the weapon is a commendable backpacker or prepper rifle."
msgstr ""
"大型の競技用銃と同等の機能をバックパック程度のサイズに凝縮した、コンパクトで軽量なボル"
"トアクションライフルです。伸縮可能な銃床に加え、.223口径レミントン弾とソ連製7.62x39mm弾"
"どちらにも対応できる交換可能な銃身が備わっており、旅人やプレッパーには打ってつけのライ"
"フルと言えます。"

msgid "Compare"
msgstr "比較"

msgid "Compare recipe to item in inventory"
msgstr "所持アイテムと比較"

msgid "Compare two items"
msgstr "アイテム比較"

