msgid "Jury-rigged body armor made from thickly-stacked paper and rolls of duct tape."
msgstr "厚く重ねた紙にガムテープを巻き付けて作った粗末な鎧です。"

msgid "Just Walter Mattheau and Jack Lemmon."
msgstr "ただのウォルター・マッソーとジャック･レモンです。"

msgid "Just a big brick wall."
msgstr "大きなレンガの壁です。"

msgid "Just a broken hard drive containing the archives of Nerth Pork."
msgstr "Nerth Pork誌のアーカイブデータが入っている壊れたハードディスクドライブです。"

msgid "Just a curious traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "ただの好奇心旺盛な放浪者だよ。調子はどう？"

msgid "Just a glass of water, please."
msgstr "水を一杯。"

msgid "Just a man selling an albatross."
msgstr "アホウドリを売っているだけの男です。"

msgid "Just a moldy loaf of bread."
msgstr "カビたパンです。"

msgid "Just a monitor with the blue element burnt out."
msgstr "青色素子が壊れたモニターです。"

msgid "Just a pincushion."
msgstr "針山です。"

msgid "Just a sec, got something I need to do first."
msgstr "ちょっと待って、先にやるべきことを思い出した。"

msgid "Just a survivor, looking around.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "この辺りを通りかかった、ただの生存者だ。ここで何をしているんだ？"

msgid "Just a traveler.  Can I ask you a few things?"
msgstr "ただの旅人だよ。ちょっと質問してもいいか？"

msgid "Just a traveller, trying to survive.  What about you?  Scavenging?"
msgstr "私は生きようともがくただの旅人だ。あなたは？物資の調達？"

msgid ""
"Just about everyone is dead, but some people survived, right?  But just like you go "
"around breaking into houses and taking whatever you think you need or want, well, "
"other survivors do the same thing.  And that stack of loot you've been accumulating "
"looks just like some random dead person's loot when it's left alone.  If some other "
"scavenger comes around and sees that loot, and you or I or another ally isn't around "
"to claim it, that other survivor is just going to take it.  So try to detail someone "
"to watch your stuff - whether its at a base or in a vehicle.\n"
"  Also, we've teamed up to better our chances of survival.  Other people are going to "
"do the same, forming little factions just like we did.  If you open the faction "
"manager (keybind '#'), you can see a list of all your allies, as well as all the other "
"factions you've met so far.  Some factions are really just some guy trying to survive "
"on his own, but other factions have dozens of members and fortified bases and such.  "
"You might want to find some of them and try to make friends with them."
msgstr ""
"人類はほぼ死んでしまったが、中には生き残ってる人もいる。あなたが必要な物や欲しい物を何"
"でも回収するのと同じように、他の生存者も同じことをするんだ。あなたが集めた戦利品の山"
"も、誰もいない場所に放っておけば他人からは戦利品にみえる。周りに所有権を主張するあなた"
"自身や他の仲間がいないと、他のスカベンジャーがやってきてその戦利品を勝手に持って行って"
"しまうだろう。だから、拠点だろうが車両だろうが、あなたの物資を見張る人員を用意しよ"
"う。\n"
"それと、生存確率を高めたいならチームを組もう。他の生存者も、同じように小さな派閥を形成"
"している。派閥メニュー(#キーを押す)では、これまでに出会った全ての派閥を一覧で確認でき"
"る。派閥と言っても、実際はただ生き残ろうとして集まっただけの人々もいれば、要塞化した拠"
"点で暮らす数十人の集まりもある。他の派閥の一員を見つけて、交流を深めておくといい。"

msgid "Just an autographed copy of the Kama Sutra."
msgstr "サイン入りカーマスートラです。"

msgid "Just an ordinary pair of rollerblades."
msgstr "一般的なローラーブレードです。"

msgid "Just another <shitty> tale of love and loss.  Not one I like to tell."
msgstr "ありきたりな愛と喪失の<shitty>物語だよ。その話はしたくないんだ。"

msgid "Just another survivor.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "ただの生存者だ。ここで何をしているんだ？"

msgid "Just because a place is dangerous doesn't mean it's worth looting."
msgstr "危険な場所だからと言って、素敵な戦利品があるわけではありません。"

msgid ""
"Just because they're not boots on the ground doesn't mean they aren't helping.  In "
"fact, I'd say that a lot of them are our most important people.  They keep the power "
"running, for one thing.  And even if they weren't helping, look at it this way: all of "
"us are scared, and almost all of us have lost someone from all this.  We aren't going "
"to throw our own to the wolves."
msgstr ""
"外で活躍していないからといって、役に立っていないわけじゃない。むしろ、下の階の住人こそ"
"が、俺らにとって一番重要な人材なんだ。電力の維持も任せているしな。たとえ役に立たない住"
"人だったとしても、ちょっと考えれば分かるだろ。俺らは、仲間をオオカミの群れの中に放り込"
"むようなことはしない。"

msgid ""
"Just bought some of this new \"Free Whiskey\" from the caravaneer up above.  It's vile "
"if you ask me, but it packs a good punch.  A real drink of the apocalypse I suppose."
msgstr ""
"そうそう、行商人から「フリー・ウイスキー」ってのを新しく仕入れたんだ。味は下品だけど、"
"パンチが効いてる。文明崩壊に似合いの酒だね。"

msgid "Just bring it to me when you have it."
msgstr "見つけたら持ってきてくれ。"

msgid "Just bring them to me when you have it."
msgstr "手に入れたら、俺のところに持ってきてほしい。"

msgid "Just fine.  Nice of you to ask.  How's it going, <granny_name_g>?"
msgstr "元気よ。お気遣い感謝するわ。<granny_name_g>、そちらはどう？"

msgid ""
"Just flipping through the book, I can tell that one ingredient in most of the "
"alcoholic drinks that we don't have a large supply of is sugar.  What alcohol we have "
"been able to loot isn't going to last us long, so starting our first large batch is a "
"priority.  Could you bring in 80 lbs of sugar?  That should last us until we can start "
"producing our own supply."
msgstr ""
"例の本をパラパラと見していて気付いたんだが、大抵のアルコール飲料は、材料に大量の砂糖が"
"必要だというじゃないか。ここに砂糖の備蓄はほとんど無いんだ。拾ってきた酒だけではすぐに"
"立ち行かなくなってしまう。砂糖を80単位持って来てくれないか？それだけあれば、自力で最初"
"の一杯を醸造するまではなんとかなるだろう。"

msgid "Just follow your map."
msgstr "マップを見て進むんだ。"

msgid "Just for fun."
msgstr "単なる娯楽用品です。"

msgid "Just give me my wrench."
msgstr "いいからレンチを取ってくれ。"

msgid "Just glad to help."
msgstr "お役に立てて嬉しいよ。"

msgid "Just go down to the Terminal if you want in."
msgstr "ターミナルへ行きたいなら、さっさと行けって。"

msgid "Just gotta stay calm, and you'll make it through this."
msgstr "ちょっと落ち着きましょう、これさえあれば大丈夫です。"

msgid "Just in case - how else can I tell you to stay put?"
msgstr "念のため聞いておくけど、その場でじっとしてほしい時はどう指示すればいい？"

msgid "Just leave me alone."
msgstr "放っておいてくれ。"

msgid "Just leave, this isn't right at all."
msgstr "立ち去ろう、何かがおかしい。"

msgid "Just let me know if you change your mind."
msgstr "もし気が変わったら教えてよ。"

msgid "Just let me know what you need."
msgstr "もし気が変わったら教えてよ。"

msgid ""
"Just like a cat, you are quick, agile, and hard to pin down.\n"
"\n"
"+1.0 Dodging skill.\n"
"Lasts 2 seconds."
msgstr ""
"ネコのように素早く身軽に動き、束縛を拒絶します。\n"
"\n"
"回避スキル+1.0\n"
"２ターン継続"

msgid "Just like all the sinners, roaming through Hell."
msgstr "地獄をさまよう罪人と同じように、ですか。"

msgid ""
"Just like bubbe used to have at the Seder.  A true classic of the Jewish people "
"despite its origin as a marketing tactic to sell coffee, the Maxwell House Haggadah "
"has sold millions of copies and graced the Passover tables of millions of families."
msgstr ""
"過越祭で振る舞われていたバブカと似たようなものです。マックスウェルハウス・ハッガーダー"
"はコーヒーを売るためのマーケティング戦略として誕生したにもかかわらず、ユダヤ教徒の伝統"
"的な正しい祈祷文とされており、何百万部も販売され、過越祭の日に家庭の食卓を飾っていまし"
"た。"

msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks and an "
"additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but it's still "
"susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""
"一般的な木製の扉ですが、木材が釘で固定され、補強のために蝶番が追加されています。頑丈さ"
"は増したものの、燃えやすさは元のままです。"

msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks for "
"reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but it's still susceptible to fire.  It's open, "
"so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr ""
"一般的な木製の扉ですが、複数の木材を釘で打ち付けて補強してあります。頑丈さは増したもの"
"の、燃えやすさは元のままです。大きく開いている今の状態では何の障壁にもなりません。"

msgid "Just like that?"
msgstr "それだけ？"

msgid ""
"Just looking at this thing makes you feel like a proper mad scientist.  It's a series "
"of glass tubes and round flasks, connected to a central motor and a heating element.  "
"The heating element warms one flask, kept rotating by the motor, evaporating the "
"contents.  The vapor is then condensed in the tubes and collected in another flask, in "
"case you wanted to save it for later."
msgstr ""
