msgid ""
"SOYPELUSA SUITS FIND NEW AMMO:  Following the infamous disaster of the DaiZoom product "
"launch and the numerous lawsuits that sprung from its failure, research from Harvard's "
"Cognitive Neuropsychology labs has brought new evidence in the ongoing litigation "
"against the company.  We spoke with lead researcher Doctor Soren Eldridge who had this "
"to say: \"The DaiZoom bar, beyond its notoriously bad taste, appears to cause in its "
"consumers symptoms similar to those of a major depressive disorder.  There is an "
"actual tangible impact on mood that lasts well beyond the initial consumption of even "
"just a few bars in a short span of time - we suspect DaiZoom may actually be "
"chemically inhibiting dopamine receptors.  This is unprecedented, and quite exciting, "
"given that it consists entirely of otherwise biochemically bland ingredients.\"  "
"Doctor Eldridge stated that further research would be needed to determine the full "
"extent of the issue and whether consumption of DaiZoom had long-term health effects "
"similar to existing dopamine blocking drugs, and if there is any role for it as a "
"medical therapy in the future.  The full interview can be found on page 7."
msgstr ""
"『SOYPELUSA訴訟に新展開』ダイズームの発売中止に伴いSOYPELUSA社に対して提起された複数の"
"訴訟において、ハーバード大学認知神経心理学研究所の研究が新たな証拠として提出されまし"
"た。主席研究員のソレン・エルドリッジ博士にお話を伺いました。「ダイズームバーはその不味"
"さで悪名を轟かせていますが、それだけでなく摂取者に重度のうつ症状を引き起こす可能性があ"
"ります。短時間にバーを数本摂取した際の心身への影響は、一本だけ摂取した場合と比べてはる"
"かに長期間に及ぶのです。つまり、ダイズームにはドーパミン受容体を阻害する化学的作用があ"
"ると、我々は考えています。この食品が生化学的にまったく問題のない成分だけで構成されてい"
"ることを考えると、極めて特異で興味深い研究結果です」この問題の全容、そしてダイズームの"
"摂取が既存のドーパミン遮断薬と同様に身体へ長期的に影響を及ぼすのか、医学療法への活用可"
"能性といった点について、エルドリッジ博士は更なる研究が必要であると述べています。7頁にイ"
"ンタビュー全文を掲載。"

